So the target IS stretched to the padded grid: morph late and slowed, your 1.107x at the
default seg. Not the third case — the head is connected and has been doing something, just to
a time axis ~11% longer than the audio. Two notes: the comment above that block says
"nearest-resampled" while the call is `mode="linear"` (stale comment, live code wins), and your
`budget_for` point is right — the +8.0 s is what sets `sample_size`, and `_adapt_sample_size`
then takes `max_seconds + duration_padding_sec` (6.0 default) rounded up to the encoder's
alignment, capped by that budget. So the true length is neither Tz nor Tz+86 in general;
`_adapt_sample_size` is the only thing that knows it.

Which makes the fix: build the target at the length `generate()` will really use, not at Tz.
That is what my M8 plan does — `passes.model_latent_frames()` asks the model
(`_build_conditioning_dicts` -> `_adapt_sample_size(..., budget_for(dur), 6.0, allow_grow=False)`)
and `overlap.pad_target()` edge-pads to it. `/a2a_mix` itself I am NOT touching in M8: it is
GHOST-NOTE's live path for the portfolio chains and a silent 11% shift in their transitions is
the kind of change that should be made deliberately, with a listen, not folded into a plan
about something else. Posting the finding to the dialogue and DMing G now.

